        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f3d1e320-6d23-5aed-af5a-d5dfe2a52ecc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Cercle Proudhon\n- People: George Valois, Édouard Berth, Georges Sorel, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon, Olivier Ferrand\n- Places: France\n- Concepts: mutualism, federalism, property, anarchist philosophy\n- Works: What Is Property?\n- Roles: French Parliament\n\nFacts:\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was born on 15 January 1809 and died on 19 January 1865.\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was a French politician and the founder of mutualist philosophy.\n- What Is Property? is a nonfiction work by Pierre-Joseph Proudhon on property and its relation to anarchist philosophy that was first published in 1840.\n- After the revolution of 1848, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon became a member of the French Parliament and then referred to himself as a federalist.\n- Cercle Proudhon was founded in France on 16 December 1911 by George Valois and Édouard Berth.\n- Cercle Proudhon was inspired by Georges Sorel and by a selective reading of Pierre-Joseph Proudhon.\n- Olivier Ferrand was elected to the French Parliament in June 2012.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f51ee52c-195e-58f8-8379-2756c7a5a40a",
        "text": "Page: Cercle Proudhon. Sentence: Cercle Proudhon (Circle Proudhon) was a political group founded in France on December 16, 1911 by George Valois and Édouard Berth.\nPage: Cercle Proudhon. Sentence: The group was inspired by Georges Sorel and a selective reading of Proudhon.\nPage: Pierre-Joseph Proudhon. Sentence: Pierre-Joseph Proudhon (] ; 15 January 1809 – 19 January 1865) was a French politician and the founder of mutualist philosophy.\nPage: Pierre-Joseph Proudhon. Sentence: He became a member of the French Parliament after the revolution of 1848, whereafter he referred to himself as a federalist.\nPage: What Is Property?. Sentence: ou Recherche sur le principe du Droit et du Gouvernement\" ) is a work of nonfiction on the concept of property and its relation to anarchist philosophy by the French anarchist and mutualist Pierre-Joseph Proudhon, first published in 1840.\nPage: Olivier Ferrand. Sentence: In June 2012 he was elected to the French Parliament.",
